description:
FILED s515a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-11) from the #3184 oracle (review/p515a/tagimport.pl).

    use FindBin; use lib "$FindBin::Bin/lib";
    use TagMod qw(:all);            # lib/TagMod.pm: sub f0 ($)
    print f0 "a", "\n";
perl: f0(a).  PCL: f0(a,\n) and a detector line -- Parser2::_premerge_include_prototypes seeds inc_paths only from LITERAL `use lib` strings (an interpolated path is run-time computed, #235), so TagMod is never found at parse time; with PERL5LIB=<that dir> the program = perl.  $FindBin::Bin IS a static fact (the script's own directory), but naming FindBin in Pl/ is the rule-9a smell: the fix needs a generic mechanism (e.g. a facts entry that says a variable is the script's directory) or a ruling.  The idiom is everywhere in CPAN t/ files and scripts.
